My latest game as a gnome healer I found an wand of wishing sitting
on the floor of level 1.  I had already been planning on pacifist
conduct (this is my umpteenth try), but this sealed the deal, and
made up for the fact that I had horrible stats and couldn't even
cast healing yet.  Wished for scrolls (got one), SDSM, CoMR and speed
boots (+0), saving the 2 remaining wishes (the wand was 0:2).

At this point I made a run for the protection racket, but my dog got
killed on the first level of the mines (I couldn't coax it away from
the monsters to heal itself, and had no leash or whistle).  Then
began some of the most difficult playing I've ever done, working my
way solo to the town and back, exploring the first level of sokoban
for the food (but unable to continue because of a werefoo there, and
on almost every dungeon level at that point).  No tripe anywhere.
Finally I wish for a =Conflict, and am able to trim down the mobs of
monsters that had been chasing me in circles.  I'm worried that if I
use the last wish for a figurine of an Archon there's still only a
4/5 chance of getting it as a pet, and further a 1/5 chance of it
killing me, so I hold off on this.  If I can get to the castle I can
assure myself of the pet.

Diving down (as a level three character), I make it to the big room,
where I finally see some tripe.  I grab it and run back before the
masses get to me, and am able to find a dog to tame.  I take him
back up as fast as I can (I've found a magic whistle by this point),
and carefully build up his levels.  I also tame a cat in the process
and build it up as well, so they're both maxed out.  We explore down
to the quest level, but I'm feeling wimpy (level 4 after I found a
!oGL), and decide to clear out mines end first hoping for some more
potions and scrolls.

There was a bones level just below minetown, which was almost more
of a hinderance than anything since it had Excalibur (useless to a
neutral pacifist and hurts if I want to wish for artifacts).  It
also had some spare potions and scrolls, and some food which I
needed (still had low stats, yet needed to keep casting to keep my
pets alive).

The bottom of the mines is the Gnome King's wine cellar, yay!  Two
chickatrices are in the room, though, which makes me nervous.  I
decide to try to line them up and hit them with my /oSleep.

  Click! You trigger a rolling boulder trap!
  You are almost hit by a boulder.  The boulder hits the hobbit!
  The hobbit is killed!

No more pacifist conduct.  The game is now worthless to me.  All
that effort, the extreme carefulness with which I had played,
ruined.  I was wielding a cream pie and using G for every move, but
one false step and it means nothing.  Worse than YAAD, and far
later in the game than any YAAD should occur (I had the AK).

All other conducts are voluntary (with the possible exception of
poly-self if you step on a polytrap, though this can be guarded
against once you have poly-control).  This should be voluntary too,
not left up to the random chance of whether you can get through all
50+ dungeon levels without accidentally hitting a boulder trap.  In
fact, the Pacifist FAQ states that if the trap isn't discovered yet
(it wasn't), you shouldn't lose conduct, but I did.  If this isn't a
bug it should be.

